{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "Which incidents warrant prioritized attention (severity/urgency signals derived from incident descriptions)",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "has_critical_keyword",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Flags descriptions containing critical-severity language, a direct signal of attention-worthiness."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_type",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Categorizes the incident domain, giving a facet to segment where attention is concentrated (Email, Database, VPN, etc.)."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_frequency_rank",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Encodes how common each issue type is, helping identify high-volume clusters worth attention; mildly redundant with issue_type but adds a prioritization dimension."
    },
    {
      "name": "contains_outage_signal",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Detects outage-related language, another concrete severity/impact indicator feeding attention."
    },
    {
      "name": "attention_score",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "An aggregate composite that directly operationalizes the focus, ranking incidents by how much attention they merit."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.88,
  "structure_quality": 0.78,
  "focus_actionability": 0.85,
  "rationale": "The columns cohere tightly around a single inferable focus: identifying attention-worthy incidents from their descriptions. Rather than a generic grab-bag or bare token counts, they form a layered structure -- textual severity signals (has_critical_keyword, contains_outage_signal), a domain segmentation facet (issue_type) with an associated volume dimension (issue_frequency_rank), and a synthesizing composite (attention_score). This is a sound predictor/facet set at a useful granularity that an analyst could act on (triage, prioritize, drill into high-score or outage-flagged incidents). Minor deductions: issue_frequency_rank appears to be a mechanical restatement of issue_type counts (redundant granularity), and attention_score's construction is opaque, so its analytical validity depends on how its inputs are combined -- otherwise it risks circular restatement of the other flags. These weaken structure_quality slightly but do not break the coherent focus."
}

